    "created_at": "2017-12-11T20:36:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-12-11T20:36:58Z",
    "body": "I think the reason we chose marshal over JSON a few months ago is performance:\r\n\r\n1. I think we originally implemented using JSON, but @idk3 found it uses too much memory, and switching to marshal reduced the memory usage by an order of magnitude.\r\n\r\n2. Another issue was that JSON requires every key (and value?) must be string, so we end up having lots of conversions from number to string and string to number, which is not efficient. \r\n\r\nThat being said, I agree JSON is more readable for very small operators when performance is not a concern. However, if you want human-readable format, is the __str__ method of the operators sufficient? @kevinsung \r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/quantumlib/OpenFermion/issues/comments/350850428/reactions",
